[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67771,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxofibrosarcoma is a malignant fibroblastic neoplasm with variably myxoid stroma, pleomorphism, and a distinctive curvilinear vascular pattern.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67772,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8811/3 Myxofibrosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67773,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B53.0 Myxofibrosarcoma, primary site</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67774,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> myxoid malignant fibrous histiocytoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67775,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid myxofibrosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67776,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxofibrosarcoma accounts for approximately 11% of chest wall sarcomas {23891404}. About 60% involve superficial soft tissues; the remainder are subfascial/intramuscular. There are case reports of cardiac myxofibrosarcoma, but it is unclear whether these are true myxofibrosarcomas {29720127}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67777,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a slow-growing mass, with or without pain.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67778,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "<p>There is a slight male predominance, with tumours occurring mainly in the sixth to eighth decades of life. It is rare in patients aged &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;years {8604805; 20878245; 26759307}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-24T17:45:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67779,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67780,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxofibrosarcomas have complex karyotypes {8604805}. Progression in grade, seen in recurrences, is accompanied by increased cytogenetic aberrations {16415793}. Gains of chromosome&nbsp;5 are common {22322669; 25384383; 28776571; 27577794}. Aberrations in p53 signalling and the cell-cycle G1/S checkpoint play a pathogenetic role in half of myxofibrosarcomas {30018380}. For additional information, see the <em>Soft tissue and bone tumours</em> volume of this series [[WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Soft tissue and bone tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2020. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 3). https://publications.iarc.fr/588.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67781,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are infiltrative, with a multinodular, gelatinous to fleshy appearance. Necrosis is often present in high-grade tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67782,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Myxofibrosarcomas have a multinodular growth pattern, with myxoid stroma, incomplete fibrous septa, curvilinear vessels, and variably pleomorphic spindled cells {8604805; 15138937}. Low-grade tumours are relatively hypocellular with low mitotic counts. Tumour cells often condense around vessels. Pseudolipoblasts containing cytoplasmic mucin are common. Higher-grade tumours are less myxoid with more solid areas and a greater degree of pleomorphism, and they may have necrosis. Higher-grade tumours often contain areas resembling low-grade tumour.</p>\r\n<p>The epithelioid subtype is composed predominantly of atypical epithelioid tumour cells and may mimic carcinoma or melanoma {17197925}. Myxofibrosarcoma may be positive for CD34 and SMA, but it is negative for desmin and S100 {23600956}.</p>\r\n<p>In the mediastinum, the differential diagnosis is nearly always with dedifferentiated liposarcoma {23020289}. Reported cardiac cases are probably undifferentiated sarcomas or intimal sarcomas (with <em>MDM2</em> amplification) {24625414}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-24T17:19:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67783,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67784,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67785,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Infiltrative tumour with multinodular architecture, myxoid stroma, variably prominent pleomorphic cells, and distinctive curvilinear vessels</li>\r\n<li>Higher-grade tumours are more cellular and may have necrosis</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67786,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) or American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67787,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 186,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is frequent local recurrence (30&ndash;40%) irrespective of grade. Metastases and mortality are closely related to tumour grade. The overall 5-year mortality rate is 30&ndash;35%. In addition to pulmonary and osseous metastases, lymph node metastases are sometimes seen {15138937; 20878245; 26759307}. The epithelioid subtype of myxofibrosarcoma is more aggressive {17197925}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:51:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]